  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a **binary** string AAA of length NNN.\n\nLet F(i,j)F(i,j)F(i,j) denote the length of **longest non-decreasing** subsequence of the substring [Ai,Ai+1,…,Aj][A_i, A_{i+1}, \\ldots, A_j][Ai​,Ai+1​,…,Aj​].\n\nFind the value ∑i=1N∑j=iNF(i,j)\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\sum_{j=i}^{N}F(i,j)∑i=1N​∑j=iN​F(i,j).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input:\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the binary string AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains AAA, a binary string of size NNN.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the required sum.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1061 \\leq T \\leq 10^61≤T≤106",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "0≤Ai≤10 \\leq A_i \\leq 10≤Ai​≤1",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2\n11\n2\n10\n5\n01110\n1\n0",
        "output": "4\n3\n31\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nF(1,1)=1F(1,1) = 1F(1,1)=1\nF(1,2)=2F(1,2) = 2F(1,2)=2, since the substring 111111 is non-decreasing.\nF(2,2)=1F(2,2) = 1F(2,2)=1\n\nThus, sum of all F(i,j)F(i,j)F(i,j) is 444.\nTest case 222:\n\nF(1,1)=1F(1,1) = 1F(1,1)=1\nF(1,2)=1F(1,2) = 1F(1,2)=1, since the longest non-decreasing subsequence is length 111. Both longest non-decreasing subsequences, 000 and 111, are of length 111.\nF(2,2)=1F(2,2) = 1F(2,2)=1\n\nThus, sum of all F(i,j)F(i,j)F(i,j) is 333."
      }
    ]
  },
